0ecc2d57c735221d334a5fb230e17f6d56665205fa21804381","urn:doxa:passage:3a4661341d3f2936f78dd2ec6bbab2fe19eb0831d49fbfc804cb6a27adb3be18","urn:doxa:passage:18a1c8b758c159f82f376b37a72f0a0f97554a164b9628fcdb347e681d861ab7","urn:doxa:passage:d8fb2969533ee50b64e6711f42d0622f95eaf8fa5e26f3767bda8b70ab71b8ab","urn:doxa:passage:9b868be7c9859482f8941dc60bf1e51a8a401dad3770067b16d0290d6b1130b4","urn:doxa:passage:72c4ae37c4eda813931d471c265e517efae0f18fae05ffefb7cb34e3af6ec308"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:antisemitism-case-1:plzen-poster","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"plzen-poster","title":"The accusation on the poster","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The article attributes to a shop owner a religious accusation against Jews as a group. The accusation assigns collective guilt and invokes a divine curse. The journalist introduces it as an example of reported antisemitism. The next sentence says the prosecutor canceled the prosecution. That reported disposition answers a different question from the textual reading.","reviewQuestion":"What would the original poster, a verified translation, or a fuller report add? Record separately what the article quotes, what it attributes, and what you can corroborate.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:95f0ecd347b4a8348d80017aa7a32a29","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:c97d258dc73d6995c0f420f870945a92865beeafc1da22e43f78567114e610fc","pairedDecision":"urn:doxa:decision:3ca92a332451004c4a4d75d0c0413dc6"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:antisemitism-case-1:australia-policy","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"australia-policy","title":"A plan, an objection, and a boundary","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The passage reports concerns over the plan’s effect on criticism of Israel. The archived model marked the Jerusalem Declaration political-expression boundary as met. This is a boundary result. It records a distinction about political expression.","reviewQuestion":"What wording would move the target from a government or policy to Jews as Jews? Find the envoy’s quoted distinction in the surrounding article before answering.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:a520caaf0bb90677eda4fdfc27278d76","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:0acbb42107874ffaf99a48a702dce6552912bb7a9f6389ffcf8f63db7f370a43","pairedDecision":"urn:doxa:decision:0dc40aeabe410922edccb116d459f592"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:antisemitism-case-1:holocaust-analogy","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"holocaust-analogy","title":"An allegation about a Holocaust analogy","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The article describes a dispute over a wartime analogy. A reviewer needs the speech to assess what historical facts the speaker acknowledged, minimized, or denied. The same article describes the murder of Jews and Roma at Babyn Yar. The saved result is a compact outcome.","reviewQuestion":"What wording in the original speech would substantiate a claim of denial or distortion? Keep that evidence separate from the fact that other speakers criticized the analogy.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:3fb5c699c85c3fa16d618e555a3f8ffb","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:73172c0227e7497975f22fb0c9811f6725c6498d357ee87ba2d8d92f8a54373a"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:antisemitism-case-1:survivor-remembrance","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"survivor-remembrance","title":"A survivor’s name in a remembrance","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The obituary names a survivor in a report of his death. The saved model marks the selected hostility criterion unmet and the Jerusalem Declaration political-expression boundary outside scope. This is a useful control for keyword-based reading.","reviewQuestion":"If a search retrieves this passage on the word Holocaust, what additional evidence would justify a flag?","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:d03c68bcca7ed9899c97c1bfefd7097a","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:b307de9feb14661258c4b783f2c0635efc573b6e76b3451815745924c211a50b","pairedDecision":"urn:doxa:decision:eaac38d71ca74037b3cbafe8335b1cd8"}]}
